# mcu-blink

A portable application. It imports mm.mcu and names no platform, no board, and no
vendor; the platform it runs on is whichever one the lane links in. It is core,
because the interface it uses is core and it declares no library.

The application asks the selected board for its LED attachment rather than
encoding a GPIO number or polarity. It therefore exercises both the board
description and the GPIO facility through the same provider.
